/*
 * BUINOKONG - a miniature arcade climber for the original MAKERbuino
 *             / Gamebuino Classic  (ATmega328P, 84x48 PCD8544 LCD, D-pad + A/B/C)
 *
 * Library : Gamebuino Classic 0.5.2 (Arduino Library Manager: "Gamebuino Classic")
 * Board   : Arduino/Genuino Uno (ATmega328P @ 16 MHz); export the *standard* HEX
 *           (NOT "with_bootloader") and name it BUINOKON.HEX  (8.3 file names!)
 *
 * Design notes
 *  - No dynamic memory, no big RAM arrays; all graphics live in PROGMEM.
 *  - Fixed-point (1/8 pixel) int16_t positions; no floating point.
 *  - The playfield is generated from tiny tables (4 sloped girders + Luna's
 *    ledge), so there is no tile map in RAM.
 *  - High score: EEPROM bytes 0..2. The Gamebuino loader mirrors EEPROM to
 *    BUINOKON.SAV when you return to the loader (hold C+A, or C on the title).
 *
 * Controls: D-pad walk/climb, A jump, B hold = swing hammer, C pause.
 * All code and sprites are original. Released under LGPL-3.0-or-later.
 */
